{
  "_doc": "What every part of the app shows or does, and the MCP tool (and answer fields) that gives an AI client the same (AGENTS.md, MCP parity: AI work is limited by the model, never by a missing tool). Checked by crates/tectora-mcp/src/parity_tests.rs: every Tauri command and every Svelte component and TypeScript module of the UI must be listed here, every tool named must exist, and every `checks` path must be present in that tool's answer for a busy test job. A new command, component or helper module fails the test until it is listed with its MCP counterpart, or with the reason it carries no information an AI needs (`user_only`, `no_data`). docs/ui-mcp-parity.md explains the rules.",

